%% DM26-0670

%% Losing the connection and coming back, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-client-reliability.md, "Step 2, as built"). Shaded is the design, not built:
%% the outbox file (step 3) and the deduplication (step 4). So a facade that ends loses its outbox, and a message sent again may be delivered twice.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant D as Domain actor
    participant F as Facade (outbox, buffer)
    participant T as Transport
    participant B as Broker

    Note over F,B: Registered. 41 and 42 were sent, and only 41 acknowledged.
    T--xB: the connection fails
    T-->>F: the transport ended: online = false, and a retry with backoff
    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over F: DESIGNED, step 3: write the unacknowledged entries to the outbox file.
    end
    D->>F: Publish (43)
    F->>F: numbered into the outbox, or the buffer when that is full, and held
    F->>T: a new transport, after the backoff
    T->>B: connect, mutual TLS, RegistrationRequest(the same registration id)

    alt the broker still has the session, and this identity and instance may resume it
        B-->>T: RegistrationResponse(Ok the same id)
    else it was ended early, its budget exhausted while it was away
        B-->>T: SessionEnded(id, why)
        T-->>D: ClientEvent::SessionEnded: the agent resynchronises
        B-->>T: RegistrationResponse(Ok a new id)
    else the broker has lost it (restarted, or the retention passed)
        B-->>T: RegistrationResponse(Ok a new id)
    else it is refused: another protocol, or a revoked certificate
        B-->>T: RegistrationResponse(Err code), and the connection closes
        T-->>D: ClientEvent::RegistrationRefused(code, reason)
    end

    T-->>F: ClientRegistered(id), which the facade sees through the transport's events
    T-->>D: ClientEvent::Registered: the builder sends each subscription again, and asks for its documents again
    F->>T: the whole outbox again, in order, with the numbers it had: 42 then 43
    T->>B: PublishRequest 42, 43
    Note over B: A broker that accepted 42 before the connection failed has no record of having done so, and accepts it again.
    B-->>T: PublishRequestAck(42), PublishRequestAck(43), each for its own message
    T-->>F: Acknowledged(42), Acknowledged(43)
    F->>F: the outbox is empty
    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over F,B: DESIGNED, step 4: subscribers drop a repeat by the origin (publisher, epoch, seq) the message carries.<br/>Today 42 reaches them twice, as at-least-once allows. And step 3: the facade removes the file.
    end
